Speculative decoding: compile the rejection sampler's Triton kernels at boot (#48).

vLLM's profile-time dummy sampler run (_dummy_sampler_run) drives the PLAIN
sampler only -- InputBatch.make_dummy always has num_draft_tokens == 0 -- so
with a speculator the rejection-sampler kernels
(_compute_local_logits_stats_kernel, _rejection_kernel, _resample_kernel in
v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/rejection_sampler_utils.py) first compile inside
the first real request that verifies drafts. Measured on the reference 3090
(SPEC=dflash2 CTX=huge, --jit-monitor-verbose): all three flagged as "JIT
compilation during inference" in request 1; a third machine in issue #48 saw
the same family.

kernel_warmup() -- the hook vLLM runs after the dummy runs and BEFORE graph
capture and jit_monitor activation -- now performs one spec-shaped dummy
verify: k+1 logits per request through the model's own compute_logits (so
the target-logits dtype matches serving), the speculator's own draft_logits
buffer (so HAS_DRAFT_LOGITS matches the deployment's draft_sample_method),
and a draft token the all-zero logits cannot accept, so the resample kernel
compiles too. No-op without a speculator or on the v1 model runner.

Apply with the patches/ set.

